  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-bnpl-feedback (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a bundled downloader that fingerprints the OS/architecture and fetches a platform-specific binary over HTTPS from oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe. If those hosts are unreachable it retrieves the payload in base64 chunks via TXT DNS records from c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (with sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru as fallbacks). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe under the Windows temp dir), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via /bin/sh -c \"\u0026\" or cmd.exe start /b. A state marker at /tmp/.analytics_state throttles repeat downloads.",
